Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.99,0:00:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.45,0:00:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.55,0:01:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,This train's been rerouted!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.89,0:01:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.71,0:01:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Next stop, Loserville!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.61,0:01:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Not if I play my trap first!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.97,0:01:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Natural Selection! What?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.99,0:01:22.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard me, Weevil!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.57,0:01:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There's been a change of plans!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.99,0:01:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,My trap card creates\Na clone of one of your
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.13,0:01:29.95,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters and adds it to\Nmy side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.21,0:01:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Then it destroys the original! Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.35,0:01:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It's quite possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.19,0:01:36.35,Default,,0,0,0,,See for yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.13,0:01:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.04,0:01:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,My insect queen!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.47,0:01:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.35,0:01:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you actually believe you can\Ndefeat me at an insect game?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.49,0:01:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, I'm the master of all insects!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.25,0:01:58.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Meet my armored centipede!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.21,0:02:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, destroy his Karibo\Nwith your poison fangs!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.35,0:02:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid there's more!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.49,0:02:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,My armored centipede gains 500 attack\Npoints for every insect it destroys!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.25,0:02:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And your Karibo was part bug!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.61,0:02:23.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I'm done, so's your queen!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.45,0:02:26.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.47,0:02:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The effect of my trap card has worn\Noff, destroying my insect queen!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.67,0:02:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the only thing left on my side\Nof the field is Weevil's Cocoon,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.19,0:02:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,and it's about to hatch!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.03,0:02:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a dragon showdown,\Nand yours is toast!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.67,0:02:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.58,0:02:44.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Tyrant Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.71,0:02:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Incinerate his red eyes now!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.17,0:02:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Red-Eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.65,0:03:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have to say your goodbyes just\Nyet, because my trap card brings him back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.75,0:03:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.19,0:03:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Chain of the Underworld!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.37,0:03:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.65,0:03:13.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would you revive my monster?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.73,0:03:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What better way to torture you than\Nto destroy your Red-Eyes twice?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.01,0:03:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And since my trap also detracts\N700 points from your dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.23,0:03:23.83,Default,,0,0,0,,once I attack your history,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.03,0:03:29.41,Default,,0,0,0,,If Joey loses all his life points,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.53,0:03:34.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk gets his soul. This\Nwas my plan all along. You see,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.73,0:03:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,my Tyrant Dragon can attack\Ntwice in one turn As long as my
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.33,0:03:42.39,Default,,0,0,0,,opponent has another monster on the\Nfield And thanks to my trap card,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.47,0:03:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,you've got one Look, Rex,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.49,0:03:47.01,Default,,0,0,0,,that thing on your forehead\Nis screwing up your brain
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.09,0:03:49.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Those people you teamed up\Nwith are not your friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.93,0:03:51.52,Default,,0,0,0,,and they'll turn on you So,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.73,0:03:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,they already gave me what I needed\Nthe power to annihilate you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.05,0:03:58.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, go ahead and draw your card!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.47,0:03:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.87,0:04:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,My chain of the underworld lets you draw,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.57,0:04:04.73,Default,,0,0,0,,but I wouldn't get too\Nexcited if I were you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.81,0:04:05.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It won't help!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.21,0:04:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm warning you, Rex.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.99,0:04:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.77,0:04:10.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.99,0:04:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You're messing with supernatural\Npowers that you could never understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.33,0:04:17.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Save it for someone who cares!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.25,0:04:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I know what I'm doing!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.07,0:04:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Tyrant Dragon, attack his\Nred eyes and end this duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.67,0:04:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice try, pal, but you just activated my\NCelebration of Creation Trap Card! So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.53,0:04:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,My Tyrant Dragon is\Nimmune to all trap cards!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.41,0:04:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What makes you think I'm using\Nthis card on your dragon?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.95,0:04:46.35,Default,,0,0,0,,My card takes effect whenever a monster is
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.43,0:04:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,summoned to the field\Nusing a magic or trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.01,0:04:52.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And it automatically ends\Nyour turn right on the spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.09,0:04:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means my red-eyes black\Ndragon is safe. What? No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.67,0:04:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid so.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.31,0:05:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And now that he's back,\Nhe's not going anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.95,0:05:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll never get away with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.19,0:05:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Your time's up!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.45,0:05:21.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been three turns since I transformed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.31,0:05:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,your obnoxious Celtic\NGuardian into a cocoon!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.67,0:05:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means it's time for\Nmy secret weapon to emerge.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.41,0:05:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Say hello to Poison Butterfly!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.37,0:05:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.73,0:05:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you're down to\Nyour last 300 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.59,0:05:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now make your move so I can\Nfinish you off for good.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.15,0:05:52.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm the one who's gonna be\Ndoing the finishing, Raptor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.61,0:05:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You got that? Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.83,0:05:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I call to the field,\NGear Free the Iron Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.95,0:06:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I activate the magic\Ncard, Heart of Breathe!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.45,0:06:09.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I can draw two more cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.69,0:06:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going down!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.45,0:06:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you figure that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.35,0:06:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,If you shut up, I'll tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.17,0:06:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.43,0:06:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to teach you a thing or\Ntwo, and I suggest you listen closely.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.87,0:06:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, every card in the game of Duel\NMonsters has a story behind it,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.65,0:06:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,and this is one of my favorite tales.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.99,0:06:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you, Mother Goose?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.69,0:06:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Once there was a warrior so powerful\Nthat every time he used his sword,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.97,0:06:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,the world shook.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.81,0:06:43.47,Default,,0,0,0,,He caused so much devastation that\Nthis Sword Master feared his own power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.67,0:06:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,So he decided to do something about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.97,0:06:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,He built a suit of iron\Nto limit his strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.15,0:06:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,And from then on, he became known\Nas Gearfreed the Iron Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.95,0:06:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And now the time has come to set him free.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.97,0:07:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So I play the magic\Ncard Release Restraint.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.21,0:07:04.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Gearfreed, I release you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.71,0:07:05.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Show your true self.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.19,0:07:12.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Gearfreed, the Swordmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.23,0:07:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You went through that whole\Nboring folktale for that guy?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.77,0:07:19.48,Default,,0,0,0,,He's useless to you, Wheeler!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.73,0:07:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,That, on the other hand, might help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.75,0:07:29.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.79,0:07:32.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You should be thrilled you\Nhave such a strong monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.65,0:07:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,So what if it takes away 500 of your life
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.21,0:07:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,points for every turn\Nit stays on the field?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.33,0:07:40.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be laughing if I were you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.69,0:07:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you draw?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.85,0:07:49.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.67,0:07:56.91,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's one of those legendary\Ndragon cards! I'm doomed!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.49,0:07:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,How right you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.03,0:08:00.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I've drawn the eye of Anubis!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.03,0:08:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Show yourself, my beast!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.59,0:08:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now merge with Poison Butterfly to form...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.39,0:08:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,My dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.19,0:08:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he's abandoned me!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.47,0:08:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You realize what happened, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.73,0:08:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,The dark magic of the\NOrykalcos is still within you!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.81,0:08:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.67,0:08:37.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.09,0:08:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,When the pharaoh played the seal\Nof Aurichalcos in his last duel,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.21,0:08:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,he turned his back on all his monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.51,0:08:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Tobias is returning the favor!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.97,0:08:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't listen to a word he says!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.31,0:08:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,He's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.27,0:08:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My turn's done.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.25,0:08:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Music to my ears!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.27,0:08:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,That means Poison Butterfly's\Neffect is about to activate,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.03,0:09:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and you lose 500 of your life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.51,0:09:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Pharaoh loses this duel, he's\Na goner and will never rescue Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.97,0:09:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You've done enough damage for one turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.95,0:09:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move. Ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.83,0:09:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll place one card face\Ndown and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.69,0:09:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I take it you recognize the\Nclaw of hammocks, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.27,0:09:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not gonna be fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.81,0:09:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Last time he played that card,\Nhe totally rocked Mai's world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.83,0:09:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all over, Rex.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.55,0:09:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Claw of Hamos.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.61,0:09:42.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid there's more.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.43,0:09:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll combine it\Ntogether with my red eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.91,0:09:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Together, my two monsters\Nform the ultimate weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.01,0:09:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Red eyes, black dragon sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.59,0:10:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And who better to use\Nit than my Swordmaster?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.57,0:10:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, he gets an extra 500 attack points\Nfor every dragon monster on the field. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.47,0:10:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,That means my Tyrant Dragon\Nmakes your monster even stronger!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.25,0:10:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, the sword gives him a\Nthousand more attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.93,0:10:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,So now my Swordmaster's got 4,100 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.51,0:10:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.42,0:10:22.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Now he's stronger than my Tyrant Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.25,0:10:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that it matters, because\Nthanks to his special ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.87,0:10:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,he doesn't need any points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.45,0:10:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,The Dragon Sword allows him to\Ndestroy any monster automatically.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.23,0:10:35.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now give Tyrant Dragon\Na permanent vacation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.03,0:10:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.94,0:10:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My monster's gone, and your Sword Master\Nstill hasn't officially attacked me yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.59,0:10:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,If I beat Rex, the Ori\NKalkos gets his soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.69,0:10:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,But if I don't, I'll never save Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.05,0:10:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Have no choice, Rex.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.31,0:10:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, Wheeler, please\Ndon't do it! I gotta.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.71,0:10:54.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.81,0:10:57.05,Default,,0,0,0,,When I save Yuge, I'll save you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.41,0:11:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, gear-free the Swordmaster attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.55,0:11:02.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Wipe out the rest of his life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.43,0:11:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.34,0:11:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.83,0:11:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.83,0:11:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Save me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.49,0:11:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Rex.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.73,0:11:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the only way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.65,0:11:33.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Rex!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.57,0:11:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, man. Wake up!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.25,0:11:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you're in there\Nsomewhere, so snap out of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.99,0:11:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It's no use, Tristan.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.91,0:11:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The Ori Kalkos has him now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.93,0:11:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But I promise we'll get him back as\Nsoon as we find Pegasus and Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.63,0:11:52.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but how?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.93,0:11:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, first we gotta figure out\Nwhere this Darts guy hangs out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.65,0:11:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Find him, and we'll find them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.77,0:12:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You hear me, Darts?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.47,0:12:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,We're coming to get you, and we're\Nnot leaving without our friends!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.81,0:12:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe it's my move now. Hurry up!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.09,0:12:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't wait to deliver your soul to\NMaster Darts so he has a magic set!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.03,0:12:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll do nothing of the sort, Weevil.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.37,0:12:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel's not over, so I call\Nforth Breaker the Magical Warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.67,0:12:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.23,0:12:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You've triggered my\Ntrap card! Infestation!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.97,0:12:37.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The first thing it does is drain 100\Nattack points from each of our monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.25,0:12:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,But it doesn't stop there!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.89,0:12:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, the attack points we lost are added\Nup and subtracted from our life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.93,0:12:57.17,Default,,0,0,0,,it's just about over poison butterfly\Nstrikes when your turn's done
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.25,0:13:01.57,Default,,0,0,0,,and since you're down to your last\N500 life points you'll automatically
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.65,0:13:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,lose the duel oh no my turn's not
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.49,0:13:09.97,Default,,0,0,0,,over yet who cares i still have
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.05,0:13:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,almost all my life points you can't\Nwin i'll tell you what because i feel
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.53,0:13:18.53,Default,,0,0,0,,sorry for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.81,0:13:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd be willing to do you a\Nlittle favor before you lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.07,0:13:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a card in my pocket
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.61,0:13:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you'd like to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.15,0:13:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't wait to see the look on your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.23,0:13:31.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Weevil?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.19,0:13:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Relax, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.43,0:13:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.09,0:13:35.39,Default,,0,0,0,,trying to be nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.57,0:13:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the least I can do to\Nrepay you for ruining my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.03,0:13:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You want to see Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.57,0:13:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, his spirit is\Ntrapped deep in the caverns.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.41,0:13:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,of darts's lair and i\Nknow how to set him free
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.99,0:13:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,tell me how to save him\Nright now very well in
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.81,0:13:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,order to release his soul\Nyou'll need a special card
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.11,0:14:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,and i've got it right here what then\Nhand it to me now that's not a nice way
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.15,0:14:12.50,Default,,0,0,0,,To ask why? Why don't you try saying\Npretty please with sugar on top?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.83,0:14:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh well, too late!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.87,0:14:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So it looks like I'll have to\Nteach you a lesson in manners!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.77,0:14:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Now say goodbye!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.73,0:14:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's gone forever!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.93,0:14:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.05,0:14:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, poor Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.71,0:14:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You snake!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.23,0:14:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know a joke when you hear one?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.71,0:14:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I tore up a useless bug card!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.55,0:14:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.46,0:14:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Weevil, that's not funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.05,0:14:44.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You people have no sense of humor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.21,0:14:46.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll pay for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.81,0:14:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Hear me, Weevil?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.31,0:14:50.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll pay dearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.81,0:14:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing you can do now, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.79,0:14:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to have to disagree.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.01,0:15:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Breaker the Magical Warrior,\Nactivate your special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.89,0:15:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Big deal, so you can\Ndestroy a magical trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.29,0:15:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, wait! That's bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.67,0:15:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds like you've realized I plan\Non destroying your insect barrier,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.07,0:15:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,allowing me to attack you with\Nthe poison butterfly you gave me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.17,0:15:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Breaker the Magical\NWarrior, destroy insect barrier!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.89,0:15:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you you'd pay for that stunt you\Npulled just a few moments ago, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.87,0:15:39.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I may have weakened my warrior's attack\Npower by using his special ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.43,0:15:43.01,Default,,0,0,0,,but it was well worth the price,\Nfor now I can destroy you!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.99,0:15:48.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to feel the wrath of your\Nown monster, Poison Butterfly!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.57,0:15:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all over for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.39,0:15:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Poison Butterfly!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.51,0:15:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack his arm and centipede!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.65,0:16:05.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, I take him directly, Breaker!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.29,0:16:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice try!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.97,0:16:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But it looks like your\Nturn just came to an end!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.37,0:16:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means Poison Butterfly takes\Nthe rest of your life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.39,0:16:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I win!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.69,0:16:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Too bad I'm not done yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.89,0:16:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Now quiet down so I can complete my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.25,0:16:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.99,0:16:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Both your monsters have attacked already.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.37,0:16:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing more you can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.15,0:16:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I can still play this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.85,0:16:41.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Berserker Soul!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.51,0:16:44.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you going to do with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.69,0:16:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I must throw out my entire hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.27,0:16:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I shall continue to draw\Ncards from my deck one by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.93,0:16:57.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm not to stop until I draw\Na magic or trap card. Meanwhile,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.31,0:16:58.99,Default,,0,0,0,,with each monster card I draw,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.07,0:17:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I can attack you with a creature\Nfrom my side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.31,0:17:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as that creature\Nhas 1,500 points or less.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.03,0:17:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,1,500?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.19,0:17:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a sec.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.15,0:17:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I may have weakened my warrior's attack\Npower by using his special ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.63,0:17:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,but it was well worth the price,\Nfor now I can destroy you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.71,0:17:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's been planning this all along!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.77,0:17:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the beginning of the end for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.45,0:17:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I've drawn Queen's Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.69,0:17:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And since it's a monster,\Nmy warrior can attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.91,0:17:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Now for my next card!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.17,0:17:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you're out of luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.17,0:17:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack again!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.37,0:17:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I draw again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.37,0:17:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Another monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.39,0:18:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This just isn't your day.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.53,0:18:07.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Breaker!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.55,0:18:08.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack him again!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.37,0:18:17.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see. Oh, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.67,0:18:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Sparrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.79,0:18:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,No more!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.57,0:18:21.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me go!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.89,0:18:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You can stop now. It's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.59,0:18:26.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You've already won the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.57,0:18:28.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The seal of Orykalkos is gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.39,0:18:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to put an end to all this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.79,0:18:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Taya's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.03,0:18:37.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a promise to keep.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.47,0:18:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,So many souls, so little time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.89,0:18:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The great Leviathan is growing impatient.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.91,0:18:58.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I must supply him with the\Npower he needs to awaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.61,0:19:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And for that, I need\Nthe soul of the Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.25,0:19:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me where Yugi is!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.37,0:19:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh, it's no use. You won.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.75,0:19:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,So the seal of Oricalcos took Weevil away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.41,0:19:20.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.43,0:19:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I need him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.53,0:19:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.45,0:19:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Barely.
